      "content": "---\nid: requirement-writing\nversion: 1\n---\n\n# Requirement writing\n\nEach requirement must be:\n\n- **singular:** one independently assessable commitment;\n- **necessary:** removing it would break a traced parent or accepted decision;\n- **unambiguous:** actor, behavior, conditions, and outcome are clear;\n- **level-appropriate:** STK is stakeholder-visible; SYS is system-level and\n  solution-independent;\n- **verifiable:** its fit criterion or verification intent describes observable\n  evidence without prescribing a test implementation;\n- **rationale-backed:** rationale explains why, not a restatement of what;\n- **traceable:** every derivation uses allowed links to authorized intent.\n\nAvoid conjunctions hiding multiple obligations, vague adjectives, passive actors,\narchitecture disguised as behavior, and requirements created only for convenience.\n"
