rget at `https://github.com/taylorrowser/mdlm-iso-date-weekday-pilot`.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The normative initial source boundary is repository file `LANE-IDENTITY.md`, Git blob `7c12a15b476ef1a54b48572f3f8a616e8b1dc968`, exact SHA-256 `743f2c2ba8a5648bb8dc34396cb4ab36b401d5dc7842b9ccec4b49d5724573af`.\n- Each record is exactly ten ASCII bytes in `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Month and day are exactly two decimal digits; Gregorian validity includes leap years divisible by 4 except centuries not divisible by 400.\n- Records are separated by one LF byte. One final LF is an accepted terminator and does not create a blank record. Empty input, a leading LF, two adjacent LFs, or any other empty record is a blank-line error.\n- CRLF, bare CR, surrounding whitespace, alternate separators, shortened fields, signs, year zero, ordinal dates, week dates, timestamps, timezone suffixes, Unicode digits, impossible dates, a UTF-8 BOM anywhere, invalid UTF-8, and non-ASCII bytes are rejected without normalization.\n- On success, stdout is exactly one compact JSON object with integer members ordered `Mon`, `Tue`, `Wed`, `Thu`, `Fri`, `Sat`, `Sun`, followed by one LF; stderr is empty and exit status is 0.\n- No success bytes are emitted until the entire file is read and accepted. Any usage, I/O, encoding, blank-line, date, input-bound, or count-overflow failure leaves stdout empty, writes one stable compact JSON error plus LF to stderr, and uses a declared nonzero exit status.\n- Failure precedence is usage, open/read failure, input-byte bound, UTF-8/BOM and record framing, canonical date validity, then record/count overflow; one detected failure produces exactly one error object.\n- Output-producing input is limited to at most 1,000,000 date records. The input-byte maximum is 11,000,011 bytes, including separators and an optional final LF. Reading stops after enough bytes to distinguish oversize input: bytes beyond 11,000,011 yield `input-too-large`. After complete framing and canonical date 